Subject: Sion East - Branch Visit Report


Sion East Branch

Visit on 12.03.26 by Kumar Ashish



Strengths:

  *   Branch has grown 15 crs in deposits this year, reaching a deposit bas=
e of 51 crs.
  *   Deposit Growth is 6.5 crs in SA, 2.5 crs in CA and 6 crs in FD.
  *   BM, Shahbaz, is experienced and a team builder.
  *   DBM, Neha, is experienced and committed to good customer service.
  *   The branch has sufficient space over ground and 1st floor.
  *   3 RM PAs in the branch are committed resources.



Challenges:

  *   Branch is making a loss of Rs.50 lakhs this year

Opportunities which need to be tapped:



The branch needs to build a comprehensive =93micro-market=94 opportunity pl=
an and then divide the execution amongst the staff. Supervisors (Cluster He=
ad and ZH) need to build capability in the team customized to the micro-mar=
ket plan and monitor progress.



In the absence of a micro-market approach, the RM PAs are sourcing their ne=
w accounts from their references. The BM is supporting and reviewing the te=
am but the leads are largely coming from the RM PAs references from the pas=
t in different catchments. New business of BBG was sourced by a customer kn=
own to an RM PA from Vashi.



The micro-market opportunity identified in discussion with the team are the=
 following:



Weekly Housing Society Activity:

  *   Senior Citizens in CHS catchment of Sion and Matunga (pre-dominantly =
of Gujarati and Tamil community) is a good opportunity for SA and FD (with =
RBL=92s higher interest USP). The branch has a monthly budget of Rs.10,000/=
- for activities, which can be well utilized for focused activities for Guj=
arati and Tamil festivals.
  *   The several CHS, in the area, also provide an opportunity for society=
 maintenance accounts. Effort has to be made by the BM and DBM to access th=
e society treasurers and pitch RBL=92s Money Multiplier product.



Small Businesses:

  *   Market of auto spare parts and mechanic shops can be tapped for CA, w=
ith the POS machine and QR codes. BIL and Small LAP can also be sourced fro=
m this catchment. Entry needs to be made into the =93association=94 with re=
lationship approach.
  *   Transport market including C&F agents: Transporters can be tapped for=
 CA, prepaid fuel cards, BBG WC facilities, LAP. Some of these C&F agents a=
lso need trade & Fx facilities for their exports.



Institutions: Catchment of schools & temples. Schools should be tapped with=
 Fees solution and temple trusts for FDs with the higher interest rates of =
RBL.



Enablement Required:



Training:

  1.  The BM has not undergone any formal class room training in the last y=
ear on any of the asset products. He has not accessed the app based BBG lea=
rning tool. We need to plan a one day classroom training for all BMs in bat=
ches =96 half day for BAT and half day for BBG. These can help in branch ge=
tting Asset led Liabilities.
  2.  The next round of classroom training should be conducted for the SDMs=
 for BBG and BAT. There are only 10 walk-ins in a day and 7 of which are be=
arers. The SDMs are experienced and can approach existing customers for cro=
ss-sell.
  3.  The next round of classroom training should be conducted for the Segm=
ent RMs and the RM Pas for BAT and BBG. These can help them in getting Asse=
t led Liabilities and other Fee income for the branch.
  4.  In branch training which was envisaged during the calendarized mornin=
g huddle by the visiting subject matter expert is not happening. The calend=
arized morning huddle is not being practiced. The BM does have a practice o=
f discussing a topic eg. CA on a certain day with the team.



Workshop: For the BMs to familiarize them with the micro-market approach.





Additional Decision to be taken immediately for this specific branch:



It=92s an un-necessarily large branch (over 1700 sq. ft carpet over ground =
and 1st floor) for a small 6 member team and 10 customer walk-ins a day. Br=
anch rental of Rs.7 lakhs per month can be saved by 50% by moving into a br=
anch of half the size.



regards, Ashish



